Yo, check the mic, one two, let me break it down for you,
About the Fed, the big boss, the one who runs the crew.
You know the game, right? The hustle, the grind,
But who controls the flow? Who’s behind the line?

It’s the **Federal Reserve**, yeah, they hold the keys,
To the whole economy, moving with ease.
Think of ‘em like the DJ, spinning the track,
If the beat gets too fast, they gotta pull it back.

See, when the money’s flowing like a river in spring,
And prices go up, making everyone sing,
The Fed steps in, says, "Hold up, chill,"
They raise the rates, make the borrowing real.

Higher rates mean loans cost more, see?
So you don’t buy that whip, you don’t buy that tee.
Spending slows down, the heat cools off,
That’s how they keep the market from getting too rough.

But if the game is slow, and nobody’s spending,
The Fed drops the rates, keeps the money extending.
Cheap loans, easy cash, get the people to move,
Buy houses, start businesses, get back in the groove.

They’re the **Bankers’ Bank**, yeah, that’s their role,
Keeping the system stable, keeping it whole.
If a big bank trips, falls on its face,
The Fed steps in, saves the whole place.

No bailouts for you, nah, that’s not the deal,
But they keep the pipes clean, keep the money real.
They print the bills, but they don’t do it wild,
They watch the inflation, like a hawk, like a child.

So next time you hear "The Fed raised rates,"
Don’t panic, homie, don’t hesitate.
It’s just the DJ adjusting the sound,
Keeping the economy steady on the ground.

They ain’t your enemy, they ain’t your friend,
Just the referees making sure the game don’t end.
So keep your head up, keep stacking that paper,
And respect the Fed, the ultimate player. 🎤🔥💸 [end of text]


